{
  "name": "custom-element-registered-through-a-wrapper",
  "description": "A class a call hands to a wrapper whose parameter reaches the platform's customElements.define is registered: a function, an arrow function bound to a variable or to a property of an object literal, a function expression bound to a variable, a method, one with a this parameter, a wrapper calling another wrapper, a wrapper called through an import that renames it, a rest parameter spread into the call, an array a variable holds spread into the call, a conditional or a nullish-coalescing argument, a wrapper held by a property of an object literal, a class field, a shorthand property or a renamed destructured binding, a wrapper reached through a parameter typed as it, an array destructuring, a call's result or a later assignment, an arrow function with no name of its own held in an array, a conditional inside an array or an object literal argument, and a conditional argument to customElements.define itself, so the reaction callback the registry calls is retained. A class handed to a function that registers nothing keeps its callback reported.",
  "rules": [
    "references-ts.38",
    "references-ts.39"
  ],
